          "heading": "Manny Feyi-Waboso on track for Australia Test despite hamstring tweak",
          "body": "England wing Manny Feyi-Waboso is on track to play Australia in the Nations Championship despite tweaking a hamstring for Exeter against Newcastle, the Guardian reported on 14 October. Initial scans showed no major damage, and Exeter's director of rugby Rob Baxter said his physios had flagged no sign of a long-term issue. Feyi-Waboso will miss Exeter's Champions Cup opener at Toulouse, and Baxter said he would take a break, with the picture changing only if the discomfort lingered at the next check."
